===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|burjon}}, {{m|enm|burioun||shoot, bud}}, from {{etyl|xno|en}} {{m|fro|burjun}}, {{m|fro|burgeon}}, {{m|fro|burgon}} (compare {{etyl|fro|-}} {{m|fro|burjon|}} "a bud"), from Old {{etyl|frk|en}} {{m|frk|*burjo||sprout, offshoot, descendant}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*burjô||sprout, descendant, offshoot}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*beraną||to carry, bear}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*bʰer-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*bʰrē-||to bear}} (cf. Albanian {{term|buron||sprout, spring, gush out}}). Akin to {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|burjan||to push up, raise}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|byrian||to come up, occur}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|byre||child, son, descendant}}. More at {{l|en|bear}}.

Alternate etymology derives {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|burjon||bud}} from {{etyl|VL.|en}} {{m|la|*burrionem}}, accusative of {{m|la|*burrio}}, from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{m|la|burra||wool, fluff}} (presumably from the down covering certain buds).

